  "content_en": "On a winter afternoon, the sun shone lazily on the carved red lattice windows of Wen Mansion, making it soft and quiet. \"Girl, Aunt Xu from my aunt's side is here!\" Sister Jiu was sitting at the yellow pear wood square table embroidering a koi picture. At this time, the door of the room was pushed open, and Qing Tao walked in with a woman wearing a purple round-collared narrow-sleeved jacket and a kind face. \"Oh, aunt, please come in quickly!\" Sister Jiu quickly stood up to greet her. \"Auntie, please sit down!\" Qing Xing, who was sitting on the other side of the table, also put down the things in his hands and brought Jin Piao over. \"Qing Xing, take a bowl of the Lao Jun Meizhong that my mother rewarded the day before yesterday and give it to my aunt to try!\" Sister Jiu ordered Qing Xing again. \"It's better not to give it up, girl!\" But Aunt Xu quickly stopped her, \"The third lady rewarded her with a good thing, so you should keep it and drink it. I don't know how to taste it. Besides... I couldn't sit still, so I just came over to pass a message to my aunt.\" \"Oh, how is my aunt?\" Sister Jiu asked immediately. \"Don't worry, girl. Not only have my aunt's kitchen delivered hot meals these two days, the dishes are also better than before. My aunt hasn't complained about feeling unwell these two days.\" Aunt Xu immediately said with a smile. \"Really, then I'll be relieved.\" Sister Jiu couldn't help but breathed a sigh of relief after hearing this. Money can make the world go round. It seems that this is true everywhere! Whether it was the rapidly developing modern society in the previous life, or the deep courtyard of the noble family today. She was originally an outstanding teacher at a certain university in the 21st century. She fell down from a building to save a student who committed suicide. Unexpectedly, when she opened her eyes, she found that she had become the ninth girl of the literary family of Ningpinghou Mansion in Bianzhou City, Dai Viet Dynasty. It was originally a very lucky thing to live a new life as a daughter-in-law again, but unfortunately this daughter-in-law has a special status, a concubine! Sister Wenjiu's father, Wen Chonghu, the third master of the Wen family, was originally a concubine, and Sister Wenjiu was the concubine of this master. Moreover, her biological mother, Aunt Xu, was still a rough girl. One time Wen Chonghu was drunk, so she pulled her into bed in a daze, and then she had Sister Wen Jiu, so she carried her aunt. ——You can imagine how embarrassing Sister Wenjiu is in this house, even though the most powerful person in the house, Mrs. Li, and her aunt and third wife, Mrs. Jiang, are not harsh on her. But with such an identity, among the four generations living under the same roof and complicated relationships, it is really not an exaggeration to say that her situation is not as good as that of the shameless maid and mother-in-law. Since the cool autumn, Aunt Xu suffered from gastrointestinal disease, and the doctor ordered her to eat hot food, but unexpectedly, this requirement could not be met, and the food always served in the kitchen was cold. Sometimes the little girl next to Aunt Xu would use the small stove to make tea and decocted medicine to warm it up, but that small thing was not of much use after all, so most of Aunt Xu's meals were cold leftovers, and her gastrointestinal problem lingered for a month without getting better. She was worried that it would turn into a serious problem in the long run, so she pooled all her personal money to bribe the housekeeper in the kitchen. What else can be done? In the inner house of a wealthy family, there are all kinds of darkness and unwritten rules... Of course, they are also the most realistic! \"Girl, my aunt asked me to deliver this!\" Aunt Xu suddenly said again, handing over a purse as she spoke. \"This...\" Sister Ninth was startled. But Aunt Xu had already opened the purse, and it contained dozens of official tickets. \"Where did this come from?\" Ninth Sister's eyebrows were deeply frowned. \"Aunt Xu said...\" Aunt Xu lowered her head and spoke in a natty tone, not answering Ninth Sister's question directly, \"Girl is old now, so she should buy some hairpins, rouge and the like. How can she not have some bodyguards around her, and she stays in the house all day long and doesn't have to go out, so...\" \"So I asked Auntie to pawn her three-winged warbler-feather hairpin, right?\" Ninth Sister's tone said solemnly. Aunt Xu didn't speak, just nodded. \"Auntie, take the money back and redeem the hairpin tomorrow!\" \"But... girl...\" Sister Jiu ignored her and put all the official tickets into her purse, and then stuffed the purse back to her. \"Girl...\" Aunt Xu couldn't help but choked in her voice, \"Auntie, she is blessed to have given birth to you.\" Sister Ninth couldn't help but have tears in her bright eyes. Although Aunt Xu was weak and incompetent and of low status, she was the best person to her in this other world. During the New Year and festivals, the old lady would occasionally reward her with snacks or something, but she would always be reluctant to eat them and would leave them to her. EveryThe first time she went to see her, he couldn't sit still for a while, so he kept urging her to leave. But when she did leave, she would always lean on the door and look around until she was completely out of sight. I love my daughter, but I am afraid that my daughter will have a rift with my aunt. This conflicting feeling is probably the deepest interpretation of maternal love. Every time she faces her, she always reminds her of her mother who was separated by time and space. She wonders if she is still well... \"Girl, on the way back from the slave girl just now, I met the seventh girl. The seventh girl went to the third girl's house again.\" After sitting for a while, Aunt Xu went back. Qingtao went to see her off and went to the sewing room to get some colored threads. But as soon as the little girl came back, she immediately came to the ninth sister with great interest. \"Oh, really?\" Sister Wenjiu just pursed her lips and smiled, \"What's the matter? Seventh sister and third sister have always been good friends. Now that third sister is about to get married, they naturally stay together.\" \"Good friends?\" After hearing this, Qingtao secretly curled her lips with some disdain and muttered softly. , \"It's not that...\" \"It's not what? Do you know again?\" The ancient boudoir life seems to be leisurely and comfortable, but in fact it is boring and boring. Especially for modern people like Jinchun, who does not leave the house every day and pursues female celebrities, it is really depressing. The two little confidants beside her, Qingxing is prudent and Qingtao is cheerful, but they are equally loyal and stay with her every day. They are just like a touch of color in this pale life, bringing her a lot of comfort and fun. Seeing the little girl's appearance, she couldn't help but want to tease her... \"Of course I know, not only I know, many people in the house see it, these seven girls simply think that these three girls are the eldest lady's favorite. It's the popular one in front of the old lady again, and now she talks about a good husband, so she's climbing on the pole to catch up...\" Naturally, the little girl couldn't help being amused, and she looked at her with a smile on her face, without a trace of resentment, and immediately poured out the whole thing like popping beans. \"If you don't say a few words, no one will treat you like a mute and sell you out!\" It wasn't until Qing Xinghu scolded her with a face that she stopped talking. Sister Wenjiu saw it, but she just smiled. Sister Wen Qi is one year older than her and is thirteen this year. She is beautiful and smart, but unfortunately her status is the same as hers - a concubine. The old Taijun Li family has four sons. The eldest, Wen Chongjiang, and the second, Wen Chonghe, are legitimate sons. The third, Wen Chonghu, and the fourth, Wen Chonghai, are concubines. This Seventh Sister Wen is the daughter of the Fourth Master Wen Chonghai, and she is also a concubine. Her mother was once the eldest girl next to the Fourth Master. The concubine is naturally the most humble among the noble family. If you want to stand firm without external help, you must be obedient and please, which is understandable. It's just that she is young after all, and what she does will inevitably be frivolous and criticized... \"Girl, the third girl's wedding is coming soon. What do you think we should fill in?\" At this time, Qing Xing suddenly said. These words made Miss Wenjiu's face darken for a moment. Hey, here comes the troublesome topic... Just now she didn't accept the banknote pawned by her aunt's hairpin, but it wasn't because she was rich, but because that thing was the most precious thing for this poor woman, how could she take it. After what happened today, the old lacquered wooden box at the bottom of her cabinet was completely empty. She has never missed the few February monthly exams as much as she does at this moment, but it is a pity that there are still many days before the monthly exams are issued. In fact, she has always been thrifty. She doesn't go along with the sisters' invitations, only to return the invitation. Things like hairpins, rouge, etc. are all distributed by the house and never purchased from outside, but her money is still tight. There is no way, living in this huge Marquis Mansion needs to be taken care of, and if there is a wedding or birthday, it will also need to be spent. \"Girl, how about...\" Looking at her girl's tightened brows and thin figure, Qingtao couldn't help feeling heartbroken. After thinking about it for a while, she said, \"How about... we... just fill in nothing. Anyway... where is the third girl?\" I don't need anything, don't...look at me like that, I, what I said...is telling the truth. That day Qingye told me that she went to give something to the third girl on behalf of the ancient mother-in-law. The third girl was very happy, good guy, and casually rewarded her with half a silver ingot, miss. Isn't it often said... I often say that... it's easy to paint flowers on brocade, but it's difficult to send firewood in the snow...\" \"Pfft -\" Qing Xing, who was staring at her because of her nonsense words, was amused, \"What are you talking about? It's easy to paint flowers and send firewood in the snow, people. What they say is the icing on the cake, the icing on the cake, okay?\" \"The icing on the cake is the icing on the cake...\" Qingtao was embarrassed by Qingxing's smile, and scratched her head, but still said stiffly, \"Actually...it's almost the same, haha, girl, you said...Yes or no? \"Sister Wen Jiu naturally laughed and laughed, but she sighed silently after laughing. They are both young ladies from the Hou Mansion, but their situations are completely different - not to mention that the third sister Wen, who is a direct descendant of the Hou Mansion, is her own sister and the biological daughter of the third wife, Sister Wen Shi. Who would scheme like me every day? Without him, there is no one to help. . In fact, there is no one to help. She has to take care of her own mother when necessary. Just like today... \"...it's one thing whether someone is in need or not. As a sister, it is necessary to fill the wedding box. Otherwise, it is rude. You are a big girl after all. How come you don't even understand this etiquette...\" Qing Xing on the side was because of Qing Tao's enthusiasm. Xue was mindless and kept lecturing her. After hearing this, Sister Wenjiu felt more and more depressed. In her previous life, she had always lived independently, working a stable job as a teacher and running a small craft shop. She had a good life, but she didn't expect that God would take advantage of her. She was sent here to live such a parasitic lif